# Panel 180 R5, shape 71 of the compiler-engineer's 117 (interpolation hole):
# a break before }.
# By the spec's opening paragraph, a string is one line, and the hole of an
# `f"..."` is inside one, so the line end leaves it unterminated: refused,
# exit 1.
function main()
    s = f"a {x  #~ unterminated_string #~v unterminated_string unexpected_block
        } b"
